---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import {
  UNIT_ROWS,
  VASPKIT_RESOLUTIONS,
  formatValue,
  kspacingFromVaspkitResolution,
} from '../../lib/reference/tables';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Units and conversions"
  description="The unit conversions a VASP user needs, computed from CODATA constants, and the VASPKIT resolution to KSPACING relation."
>
  <div class="container ref-page" data-pagefind-body data-pagefind-meta="module:Quick reference">
    <h1>Units and conversions</h1>
    <p>
      VASP prints stress in kBar, energies in eV and frequencies in THz; papers want GPa, kJ/mol and cm⁻¹.
      This table follows the units table of the author's Workflow Handbook (
      <a href="/references/#S-042">S-042</a>). No number on this page is typed in: each one is computed from
      the CODATA constants in the site's code (<a href="/references/#S-031">S-031</a>).
    </p>
    <div class="ref-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Unit conversions" tabindex="0">
      <table data-testid="units-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Quantity</th>
            <th scope="col">Equals</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {UNIT_ROWS.map((r) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{r.from}</th>
              <td>{r.to.map((t) => `${formatValue(t.value)} ${t.unit}`).join(' = ')}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>k-mesh resolution and KSPACING</h2>
    <p>
      VASPKIT 102 asks for a k-mesh resolution r in units of 2π/Å. The VASP tag <code>KSPACING</code> is in
      1/Å and already includes the 2π, so <code>KSPACING</code> ≈ 2π r (<a href="/references/#S-042">S-042</a>
      ). Why it matters: typing a VASPKIT resolution into <code>KSPACING</code> asks for a mesh about six
      times denser in each direction than you meant.
    </p>
    <div class="ref-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Resolution to KSPACING" tabindex="0">
      <table data-testid="kspacing-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">VASPKIT resolution (2π/Å)</th>
            <th scope="col">KSPACING (1/Å)</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {VASPKIT_RESOLUTIONS.map((r) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{r}</td>
              <td>{formatValue(kspacingFromVaspkitResolution(r))}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      See also <a href="/reference/where-to-read/">where to read each number</a> and the
      <a href="/reference/checklist/">pre-submit checklist</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
